            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "oath_settle": {
            "id": "oath_settle",
            "text": "[He is standing differently. Not better. Loaded.]\nThey are all on me. Five and my own, and they are pulling in five directions and one of them is toward you, which you will have noticed.\nNow. You have two ways to end this and I am going to describe both of them honestly because I have had eleven years to be honest.\nBreak it. Say the words and cut it and it is gone, and I live, and I am the first Reckoner in six hundred years to walk away from an oath, and everything I have been since I was nine is over. Bellorak will know. He always knows. There is no coming back into the Iron Reckoners after that and there is no coming back into being the man who kept faith.\nOr take it. That is allowed. That is the one clean transfer in the whole custom — an oath given willingly to a willing carrier, witness to witness. You would carry a vow to kill a man thirty-one years dead. It would be yours and it would never once be satisfiable and you would feel it, out there, pulling.\nI am not going to pretend I don't want you to take it. I have wanted somebody to take it for eleven years. But you should hear a man ask before you do it.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Break it. An oath to a dead man is not an oath.",
                "nextNodeId": "oath_break",
                "conditions": []
              },
              {
                "label": "Give it to me. I'll carry it.",
                "nextNodeId": "oath_take",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "oath_break": {
            "id": "oath_break",
            "text": "[The cut takes one motion and no ceremony at all, which after eleven years is the insult in it.]\n...\nHuh.\n[He looks at his hands. He looks at the tent. He looks at nothing, for a while.]\nI have been holding something so long that letting go feels like falling and I am not falling. That is going to take a while.\nI am not a Reckoner as of a moment ago. I do not know what I am. I am fifty-one and I have a trade and no oath and I think I am going to go and find out, which is a thing I stopped believing was available.\nBellorak will have felt it. Let him. He has had eleven years of me and he was never once going to give any of it back.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "sten_oath_settled",
                "value": "broken",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "ADD_FAVOR",
                "target": "BELLORAK",
                "value": "",
                "amount": -10
              },
              {
                "type": "ADD_FAVOR",
